 *   delimiter.
 * - Line (`-- ...`) and block (`/* ... *&#47;`) comments, which are dropped.
 * - Trigger bodies. A `CREATE TRIGGER` (optionally `TEMP`/`TEMPORARY`, and
 *   optionally prefixed with `EXPLAIN [QUERY PLAN]`) contains a
 *   `BEGIN ... END` body that may hold several semicolon-terminated
 *   sub-statements. The whole trigger definition — from `CREATE TRIGGER`
 *   through its closing `END` — is returned as a single element, no matter how
 *   many internal semicolons it contains.
 *
 * Each returned statement has its surrounding whitespace trimmed; whitespace
 * inside the statement body (newlines, indentation) is preserved verbatim.
 *
 * NOTE: This manual splitting is necessary because the JS bindings don't expose
 * an ergonomic way to execute multiple statements while capturing results from
 * the last one. The bindings provide:
 * - db.exec(sql) - executes multiple statements but doesn't return row data
 * - db.prepare(sql) - returns rows but only handles a single statement
